  "notes": "West leads the ♥7 against 6♥. South has 2 possible losers in spades and a possible loser in diamonds. West's unusual notrump overcall suggests at least 5-5 in the minors, making it likely that East was dealt the ♠K. South should look to find some chance for the contract besides the spade finesse.\n\nAfter winning West's trump opening lead, South should draw the outstanding trump. When both defenders follow, West can have no more than 1 spade (since he has shown up with 2 hearts and promised at least 5-5 in the minors with his 2NT overcall). The contract is now certain as long as West was dealt the ♦K (very likely considering the bidding).\n\nSouth should cash the ♣A to unblock that suit and cash the ♠A to remove West's safe exit card in spades. South continues with the ♦A and leads the ♦2 toward dummy's ♦Q. West must take his ♦K and West's forced minor suit return allows South to discard his 2 spade losers on dummy's ♦Q and ♣K.",
